# Common Guide

Summary: Shared rules of this workspace. The root `AGENTS.md` selects the task scope and the project; this guide answers which shared rules apply and routes to the topic needed for the task.

## Mandatory policy

Read [policy.md](policy.md) first. Its MUST rules bind every project and every agent in this workspace; project context may strengthen them but never weaken them.

## Topics

| Need | Read |
|---|---|
| Integration behavior of the enabled language workspaces | [tooling.md](tooling.md) |
| Template for workspace and project issues | [templates/issue.md](templates/issue.md) |
| Scaffold source for new project contexts | [templates/project/](templates/project/) |

## Projects

Project context lives at `.agents/context/<project-id>/AGENTS.md`. Registered projects are routed from the managed region of the root `AGENTS.md`; this guide never duplicates that list. A task may expressly include several projects: load the guide of every project the task names, in turn, and never read the context of a project the task does not name.

## Issues

Workspace and cross-project issues live under `issues/` when present, one Markdown file per issue following `templates/issue.md`. Issues are reached by ID or reference; never load the collection wholesale.

## GLOBAL

GLOBAL preferences are optional personal instructions the developer configures in their coding tool, outside this workspace. Agents may receive and follow them through the tool's supported loading mechanisms. This workspace neither requires, provisions, modifies nor recursively inspects personal configuration, and it functions with an empty personal profile. Applicable project settings and mandatory COMMON rules govern their respective scopes; surface material instruction conflicts for resolution instead of resolving them silently.

## Stop reading when

The mandatory policy and the one topic this task needs are known. Load only what the task names; never preload this directory.
